<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Pseudo-Code of FedSRD and FedSRD-e</h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> FedSRD and FedSRD-e Framework</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Server Initializes:</span> Global LoRA matrices <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{0},A^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{0},A^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of all clients.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initial Synchronization:</span> Each client <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> sets its local state <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}^{0}\leftarrow B^{0},A_{i}^{0}\leftarrow A^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}^{0}\leftarrow B^{0},A_{i}^{0}\leftarrow A^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each communication round <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\dots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\dots,T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
             Server broadcasts <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta B_{s}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta B_{s}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta A_{s}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta A_{s}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each client <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">in parallel</span> <span id="alg1.l6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
               Client updates local model: <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}^{t-1}\leftarrow B_{i}^{t-2}+\Delta B_{s}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}^{t-1}\leftarrow B_{i}^{t-2}+\Delta B_{s}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}^{t-1}\leftarrow A_{i}^{t-2}+\Delta A_{s}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}^{t-1}\leftarrow A_{i}^{t-2}+\Delta A_{s}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
     
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each client <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">in parallel</span> <span id="alg1.l8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta B_{i,s}^{t},\Delta A_{i,s}^{t}\leftarrow\text{ClientTraining}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>ClientTraining</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta B_{i,s}^{t},\Delta A_{i,s}^{t}\leftarrow\text{ClientTraining}(i)</annotation></semantics></math>
  
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Server-Side Reconstruction and Aggregation:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each client <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
            
            
             Client reconstructs its new state <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}^{t},A_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}^{t},A_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E4" title="In Motivation ‣ 4.1. Importance-aware Sparsification ‣ 4. Proposed Method ‣ FedSRD: Sparsify-Reconstruct-Decompose for Communication-Efficient Federated Large Language Models Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
            
            
             Server computes client’s full-rank matrix: <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}^{t}\leftarrow B_{i}^{t}A_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}^{t}\leftarrow B_{i}^{t}A_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
  
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
            
            
            Aggregate in full-rank space: <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{t}\leftarrow\frac{1}{|\mathcal{C}|}\sum_{i}W_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{t}\leftarrow\frac{1}{|\mathcal{C}|}\sum_{i}W_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Server-Side Alternating Decomposition:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{t}_{r}\leftarrow\text{SVD}_{r}(W^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>SVD</mtext><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{t}_{r}\leftarrow\text{SVD}_{r}(W^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> FedSRD-e bypasses this SVD step.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
            
            
            Let <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W^{t}_{update}=W^{t}_{r}-B^{t-1}A^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W^{t}_{update}=W^{t}_{r}-B^{t-1}A^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> For FedSRD-e, use <math id="alg1.l17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="alg1.l17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{t}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{t}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is even <span id="alg1.l18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta A^{t}\leftarrow(B^{t-1})^{\dagger}(\Delta W^{t}_{update})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta A^{t}\leftarrow(B^{t-1})^{\dagger}(\Delta W^{t}_{update})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta B^{t}\leftarrow\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta B^{t}\leftarrow\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta B^{t}\leftarrow(\Delta W^{t}_{update})(A^{t-1})^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta B^{t}\leftarrow(\Delta W^{t}_{update})(A^{t-1})^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta A^{t}\leftarrow\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta A^{t}\leftarrow\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
  
</div>
<div id="alg1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">24:</span></span>
            
            
            Update global state on server: <math id="alg1.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{t}\leftarrow B^{t-1}+\Delta B^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{t}\leftarrow B^{t-1}+\Delta B^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{t}\leftarrow A^{t-1}+\Delta A^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{t}\leftarrow A^{t-1}+\Delta A^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">25:</span></span>
            
            
            Sparsify for download: <math id="alg1.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta B_{s}^{t},\Delta A_{s}^{t}\leftarrow\text{DARE}(\Delta B^{t},\Delta A^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>DARE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta B_{s}^{t},\Delta A_{s}^{t}\leftarrow\text{DARE}(\Delta B^{t},\Delta A^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l26.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">26:</span></span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l27.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">27:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l27.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span> <span id="alg1.l27.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ClientTraining</span>(<math id="alg1.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l28.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">28:</span></span>
            
            
            Fine-tune model on local data <math id="alg1.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to get new <math id="alg1.l28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\prime}_{i},A^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\prime}_{i},A^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l29.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">29:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute local updates: <math id="alg1.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta B_{i}^{t}\leftarrow B^{\prime}_{i}-B_{i}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta B_{i}^{t}\leftarrow B^{\prime}_{i}-B_{i}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta A_{i}^{t}\leftarrow A^{\prime}_{i}-A_{i}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta A_{i}^{t}\leftarrow A^{\prime}_{i}-A_{i}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l30.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">30:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Importance-Aware Sparsification:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l31.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">31:</span></span>
            
            
            Calculate importance scores <math id="alg1.l31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\Delta B_{i}^{t}),I(\Delta A_{i}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\Delta B_{i}^{t}),I(\Delta A_{i}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E6" title="In Motivation ‣ 4.1. Importance-aware Sparsification ‣ 4. Proposed Method ‣ FedSRD: Sparsify-Reconstruct-Decompose for Communication-Efficient Federated Large Language Models Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l32.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">32:</span></span>
            
            
            Calculate adaptive sparsity ratios <math id="alg1.l32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\Delta B_{i}^{t}},\rho_{\Delta A_{i}^{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\Delta B_{i}^{t}},\rho_{\Delta A_{i}^{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l33" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l33.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">33:</span></span>
            
            
            Prune updates to get sparse <math id="alg1.l33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta B_{i,s}^{t},\Delta A_{i,s}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta B_{i,s}^{t},\Delta A_{i,s}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> adaptively.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l34" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l34.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">34:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l34.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta B_{i,s}^{t},\Delta A_{i,s}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta B_{i,s}^{t},\Delta A_{i,s}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to server.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Rationale of the Importance Score Calculation</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide the mathematical motivation for the importance score defined in Equation <a href="#S4.E6" title="In Motivation ‣ 4.1. Importance-aware Sparsification ‣ 4. Proposed Method ‣ FedSRD: Sparsify-Reconstruct-Decompose for Communication-Efficient Federated Large Language Models Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. The core idea is to quantify how much a single parameter’s change in a LoRA update matrix (<math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta B_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta B_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta A_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta A_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) contributes to the overall change in the full-rank weight matrix (<math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let’s first recall the expression of the weight update:</p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{i}^{t}=\Delta B_{i}^{t}A_{i}^{t-1}+B_{i}^{t}\Delta A_{i}^{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{i}^{t}=\Delta B_{i}^{t}A_{i}^{t-1}+B_{i}^{t}\Delta A_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We will analyze the contribution of a single element in <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta B_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta B_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to the term <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta B_{i}^{t}A_{i}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta B_{i}^{t}A_{i}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The analysis for <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta A_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta A_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A fundamental property of matrix multiplication is that the product of two matrices, <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=BA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=BA</annotation></semantics></math>, can be expressed as the sum of the outer products of the columns of <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and the rows of <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> has columns <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times k}</annotation></semantics></math> has rows <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}_{j}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}_{j}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, then:</p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=BA=\sum_{j=1}^{r}\mathbf{b}_{j}\otimes\mathbf{a}_{j}^{T}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=BA=\sum_{j=1}^{r}\mathbf{b}_{j}\otimes\mathbf{a}_{j}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This expansion reveals the structural interplay between the two matrices: the final matrix <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> is constructed from pairs of columns from <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and rows from <math id="A2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now, let’s consider the contribution of a single scalar element, <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math> (the element in row <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and column <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>), to the matrix product <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta B_{i}^{t}A_{i}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta B_{i}^{t}A_{i}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can isolate this contribution by considering a change in only this single element. The effect of this single element on the product can be represented as:</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}\cdot(\mathbf{e}_{u}\otimes\mathbf{e}_{v}^{T})\cdot A_{i}^{t-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}\cdot(\mathbf{e}_{u}\otimes\mathbf{e}_{v}^{T})\cdot A_{i}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> are standard basis vectors (vectors of zeros with a single 1 at position <math id="A2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively). Using the associativity of matrix multiplication, this becomes:</p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}\cdot\mathbf{e}_{u}\otimes(\mathbf{e}_{v}^{T}A_{i}^{t-1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}\cdot\mathbf{e}_{u}\otimes(\mathbf{e}_{v}^{T}A_{i}^{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">The term <math id="A2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{v}^{T}A_{i}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{v}^{T}A_{i}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a vector product that selects the <math id="A2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>-th row of the matrix <math id="A2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we denote as <math id="A2.p4.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(A_{i}^{t-1})_{v,:}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{i}^{t-1})_{v,:}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the contribution of the single element <math id="A2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math> to the final update matrix is itself a rank-1 matrix:</p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{Contribution Matrix}=(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}\cdot(\mathbf{e}_{u}\otimes(A_{i}^{t-1})_{v,:})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Contribution Matrix</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Contribution Matrix}=(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}\cdot(\mathbf{e}_{u}\otimes(A_{i}^{t-1})_{v,:})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.4" class="ltx_p">This matrix is zero everywhere except for its <math id="A2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>-th row, which is the <math id="A2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>-th row of <math id="A2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> scaled by the scalar <math id="A2.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">A natural way to measure the magnitude, or "importance", of this contribution matrix is to compute its Frobenius norm (<math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>). The Frobenius norm of a scaled outer product of two vectors <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|c|\cdot\|\mathbf{x}\|_{2}\cdot\|\mathbf{y}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|c|\cdot\|\mathbf{x}\|_{2}\cdot\|\mathbf{y}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. In our case, <math id="A2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}=\mathbf{e}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}=\mathbf{e}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p5.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{y}=(A_{i}^{t-1})_{v,:}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}=(A_{i}^{t-1})_{v,:}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{e}_{u}\|_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{e}_{u}\|_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the norm is:</p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I((\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I((\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\|(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}\cdot(\mathbf{e}_{u}\otimes(A_{i}^{t-1})_{v,:})\right\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>‖</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\|(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}\cdot(\mathbf{e}_{u}\otimes(A_{i}^{t-1})_{v,:})\right\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E19Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}|\cdot\|\mathbf{e}_{u}\|_{2}\cdot\|(A_{i}^{t-1})_{v,:}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}|\cdot\|\mathbf{e}_{u}\|_{2}\cdot\|(A_{i}^{t-1})_{v,:}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E19Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}|\cdot\|(A_{i}^{t-1})_{v,:}^{T}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|(\Delta B_{i}^{t})_{uv}|\cdot\|(A_{i}^{t-1})_{v,:}^{T}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This is precisely the importance score for an element in <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta B_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta B_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in Equation <a href="#S4.E6" title="In Motivation ‣ 4.1. Importance-aware Sparsification ‣ 4. Proposed Method ‣ FedSRD: Sparsify-Reconstruct-Decompose for Communication-Efficient Federated Large Language Models Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. A symmetric derivation for the term <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}^{t}\Delta A_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}^{t}\Delta A_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> shows that the importance of <math id="A2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta A_{i}^{t})_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta A_{i}^{t})_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math> is its magnitude multiplied by the L2-norm of the <math id="A2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>-th column of <math id="A2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. This formulation provides a principled way to measure a parameter’s true structural contribution to the final update, moving beyond its simple magnitude.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Description of Baselines</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our baselines span from foundational FL algorithms to advanced techniques specifically designed for communication-efficient and effective federated fine-tuning of large language models.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">FedAvg <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">McMahan et al., 2017</a>)</cite> is the first algorithm in federated learning. It establishes a simple yet effective paradigm for collaborative model training. In each communication round, clients download current global model parameters. Each client then performs multiple steps of local training on its private dataset. The resulting updated model weights are sent back to the server, which aggregates them by computing a weighted average to produce the global model for the subsequent round. FedAvg serves as the fundamental baseline for performance and communication cost.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">FedProx <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2020</a>)</cite> is a key extension to FedAvg designed to address the challenge of statistical heterogeneity (non-IID data) across clients. Non-IID data can cause local client models to drift significantly from the global consensus, leading to convergence instability. FedProx mitigates this by introducing a proximal term to the local objective function on each client. This term regularizes the local training process by penalizing the squared Euclidean distance between the local model weights and the global model weights, thereby constraining local updates and promoting more stable convergence.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">FFA-LoRA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sun et al., 2024</a>)</cite> is a parameter-efficient fine-tuning method tailored for the federated setting, focusing on reducing communication overhead and accurate aggregation. It utilizes the Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) strategy. To achieve communication efficiency, FFA-LoRA freezes the randomly initialized LoRA <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> matrices across all clients and throughout the training process. Consequently, clients only need to train and communicate the <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> matrices, drastically reducing the number of parameters transmitted in each round.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">FlexLoRA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2024</a>)</cite> proposes a more sophisticated aggregation mechanism for federated LoRA fine-tuning. It posits that directly averaging the low-rank matrices from different clients may be suboptimal. Instead, clients upload their locally trained LoRA matrices. The server first reconstructs the full-rank weight updates for each client (<math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) and averages them. Subsequently, the server performs Singular Value Decomposition (SVD) to find a new, optimal low-rank approximation, which is then decomposed into new <math id="A3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> matrices for client downloading.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">FedICU <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liao et al., [n. d.]</a>)</cite> is an advanced FL method that decomposes the global model into consensus and divergence components to handle heterogeneity better. The core mechanism is a consensus-divergence splitting performed on the server-side during aggregation. Consensus components and divergence components of all clients are aggregated separately. FEdICU further proposes the selective updating strategy that uploads only more specialized parameters for aggregation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Fed-DARE addresses the communication bottleneck in FL by integrating the DARE (Drop and Rescale) technique <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. In this approach, clients sparsify their local LoRA updates by randomly dropping parameters. The remaining non-zero elements are then rescaled to preserve the update’s expected magnitude, resulting in highly sparse matrices that significantly reduce the communication payload. We adopt a sparsity ratio of 0.9 as recommended by DARE. As shown in Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ FedSRD: Sparsify-Reconstruct-Decompose for Communication-Efficient Federated Large Language Models Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, this random-based approach outperforms magnitude-based sparsification, while higher sparsity ratios lead to performance degradation. This justifies our choice and the exclusion of magnitude-based methods as a baseline.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8. </span>Average In-domain Performance Comparison</figcaption>
